{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3444","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3444","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3444\",\"parent_revision\":\"4e9c0bdc4cc62bff6e882e10dfa941eb1724752a96143f2702dfff761ffa126c\",\"root_revision\":\"4e9c0bdc4cc62bff6e882e10dfa941eb1724752a96143f2702dfff761ffa126c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nTen SKILL.md pointers in plugin-creator write a substituted plugin path as a backticked path rather than a markdown link. That is a workaround for a skilllint false positive, not a preference, and it should be reverted when the upstream bug is fixed.\\n\\nTHE UPSTREAM BUG\\n\\nskilllint does expand the substitution variables \u2014 an earlier claim that it could not was wrong and is withdrawn. The actual defect is path joining under relative invocation: when skilllint is invoked with a relative path, its plugin-root resolution returns a relative root, and the resolved URL is then joined onto the skill directory a second time. The doubled join produces a path that does not exist, and LK001 fires.\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n\\nMeasured on the same tree, same files, differing only in how skilllint was invoked:\\n\\n- relative invocation: 2 LK001 findings\\n- absolute invocation: 0 LK001 findings\\n\\nSame files, same content. The finding count is a function of the caller's working directory, which is the signature of a path-resolution defect rather than a content defect.\\n\\nVERIFICATION AND REVERT\\n\\nWhen skilllint is fixed, confirm with the absolute-invocation run producing 0 LK001 on these files, then convert the ten pointers from a backticked path back to a markdown link, which is what the repo's markdown reference rule asks for by default.\\n\\nRelated: the same rule's exception text should be labelled Claude Code and skilllint specific, since other harnesses pass the string through literally rather than substituting it.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the bug was reported to the skilllint session during this work. Whether it was acted on has not been confirmed, so this item should not assume a fix is in progress.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: skilllint false positive investigation, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"11d25489821e680118eb36e2d5a5704f1f1c52cdc47a2f5371bd8527153a3e69\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBnGQ\"}"}